N|               The poem ends and we hear instead a RADIO BROADCAST of a             
N|               Giants' game. Mark is engrossed. Suddenly the broadcast              
N|               stops. The digital read-out on the clock radio, which says           
N,G|               12:57, disappears. A street light, visible through the               
N,G|               window, goes out. The electric pump under Mark's iron lung           
N|               whirrs to a halt. We hear the sound of air escaping, then an         
N|               eerie silence. Even the cat is motionless.                           
N|               For a few moments, Mark seems hypnotized. Then, he twists his        
N|               head and clamps onto his mouth stick. He manoeuvres it over          
N|               to the speaker button on the phone and manages to press it in        
N|               the semi-darkness. We hear a dial tone.                              
